  "tagline": "Oracle's in-memory relational database: microsecond SQL, PL/SQL, and a cache tier for Oracle Database.",
  "description": "TimesTen is an in-memory relational database that keeps the full dataset in RAM while logging and checkpointing to disk, giving microsecond-level response times for SQL and PL/SQL. It comes in two shapes: Classic, often used as a read/write cache in front of Oracle Database (Cache for Oracle), and Scaleout, a shared-nothing distributed edition. It is common in telecom charging, trading and real-time fraud checks where Oracle-compatible SQL at memory speed matters. Oracle shipped a new major line, TimesTen 26.1, in April 2026 with support to 2034, while 22.1 is supported to 2030.",
